"answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative aimed at enhancing security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole, with a kickoff scheduled for July 15th, 2023. The project involves gathering R&D proposals by July 20th to leverage AI for data visualization. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase and the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype ahead of schedule. The project budget was adjusted to $550,000 to cover real-time analytics integration, and a $15,000 training budget was approved for coding teams and project managers. Stakeholder feedback on the prototype was requested by the end of November, and security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption, were updated to take effect in January. A celebration for the milestone was held on October 10th."
